                <pb facs="0645" n="547" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg547"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. Toomey.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Washington D.
                                C.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1900-01-09"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">January 9,
                    1900</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Pennsylvania Milling and Export
                        Co.</hi>:</p>
                <p>Ambassador Choate telegraphs to-day inquiring if your flour was sold for future
                    delivery; also how does your present interest appear?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
